Simon D. Levy responded to a post about "rich getting richer,
poor getting poorer", etc. 
There is a probability distribution called Pareto distribution.
It is named after the Italian mathematician/actuary/economist
W. Pareto. Guess where it comes from? Pareto determined that
in societies studied by him, regardless of society's structure,
the distribution of wealth remains the same, i.e., Pareto
distribution. I know of no successful counterexample
(factual, not whining screaming intimidation-oriented propaganda).
